# The System's rendered voice pack (scripts/generate-voice-pack.mjs) is
# deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It was, on the reasoning that ~5 MB of cloned character audio belongs
# on the Player's own machine rather than in a public repo. That held
# right up until the app was deployed: `public/` is copied verbatim into
# the build, so keeping the pack out of git only kept it off the
# *deployment*, where the entire feature lives. Production fell back to
# the device's speech engine on every line, which is the generic voice
# this pack exists to replace.
#
# Nor did ignoring it keep the audio private. A deployed build serves
# every clip at https://<host>/voice/<id>.mp3 to anyone who asks, so the
# public exposure is identical either way — the only thing the ignore
# rule bought was a broken feature in production.
#
# Regenerate with `npm run voice`. A clip that is absent still falls back
# to the device's engine rather than to silence.

